{"id":"20260830T052731.642493004Z-51464847","time":"2026-08-30T05:27:31.642493004Z","session_id":"session-20260830T052251.276503861Z","task_id":"task-1788067371276752033","source":"system","kind":"status","summary":"Authority for this plan, by lane.\n\nrequested objective:\n  internal/report/report.go derives changed-path information by parsing diff text: it reads 'diff --git a/P b/P' headers and '+++ b/' lines. A pathname that Git quotes -- one containing a tab, a newline, a quote, or a non-UTF-8 byte -- is therefore misread or missed, and internal/workflow/engine.go's changedPaths reads through the same parser. gitx.Capture now carries an exact, NUL-parsed path set (Capture.Paths) taken after artifact exclusions. Make the change report's path information exact for pathnames Git quotes, while keeping report.Change's meaning for its existing consumers. Add tests that fail without the change.\n  NOT established as a human objective — submitted unattended; no human presence was established\n  the wording is the task; it is not a person's authorization for it\n\ntechnical claims:\n  [evidence-bearing] gitx.Capture.Paths is populated from `git diff --name-status -z` after artifact exclusions, without trimming, whitespace splitting, or rename detection. (internal/gitx/capture.go) — source: repository\n  [evidence-bearing] report.FromDiff currently derives FileChange paths from textual diff headers and therefore misses or misreads Git-quoted pathnames. (internal/report/report.go) — source: repository\n  [evidence-bearing] report.Change represents logical file changes with status and optional rename OldPath, and existing consumers depend on those semantics. (internal/report/report.go and internal/workflow/routine.go) — source: repository\n  [evidence-bearing] emitChangeReport and changedPaths currently reparse diff text through report.FromDiff even though runCandidate already holds a gitx.Capture. (internal/workflow/engine.go) — source: repository\n  [evidence-bearing] Sensei classifies the four-file scope as ARCHITECTURE_SENSITIVE with high confidence, local blast radius, and no approval gate. (planned report and workflow files) — source: graph\n  [evidence-bearing] Every report must continue to end with the claims it is not entitled to make. (internal/report/report.go) — source: graph\n  [evidence-bearing] The planned regression-test files already exist, so this plan creates no new surfaces. (internal/report/report_test.go and internal/workflow/engine_test.go) — source: repository\n  the objective does not establish any of these. Evidence does.\n\nconsequence decision:\n  BOUNDED — the candidate worktree: files are edited in an isolated checkout, the diff is audited before it leaves, and discarding the worktree leaves the world unchanged\n  assessed from the action, not from who asked and not from whether the plan satisfies the objective.\n\nrouted: architectural-authority-granted\n"}
{"id":"20260830T052731.642662692Z-c2002212","time":"2026-08-30T05:27:31.642662692Z","session_id":"session-20260830T052251.276503861Z","task_id":"task-1788067371276752033","source":"architect","kind":"plan.proposed","summary":"Use Capture.Paths as the pathname authority for live change reports while preserving report.Change’s file-status and rename semantics.\n\nPlan:\n  1. Add an exact-path-aware constructor in internal/report/report.go that preserves Change status and rename semantics while taking pathname bytes from Capture.Paths and rejecting structural mismatches.\n  2. Route the final candidate capture through that constructor in internal/workflow/engine.go and reuse the resulting Change for emitChangeReport and changedPaths without reparsing diff text.\n  3. Add report regressions for tab, newline, quote, non-UTF-8, deletion, rename, mismatch, and ordinary-path cases while retaining the existing FromDiff behavior.\n  4. Add workflow regressions proving exact quoted paths reach changedPaths and reports, with deleted paths still excluded and rename destinations retained.\n  5. Run gofmt -w cmd internal, go vet ./..., and go test ./...; report any unavailable check exactly rather than recording it as passed.","payload":{"decision":"proceed","summary":"Use Capture.Paths as the pathname authority for live change reports while preserving report.Change’s file-status and rename semantics.","steps":["Add an exact-path-aware constructor in internal/report/report.go that preserves Change status and rename semantics while taking pathname bytes from Capture.Paths and rejecting structural mismatches.","Route the final candidate capture through that constructor in internal/workflow/engine.go and reuse the resulting Change for emitChangeReport and changedPaths without reparsing diff text.","Add report regressions for tab, newline, quote, non-UTF-8, deletion, rename, mismatch, and ordinary-path cases while retaining the existing FromDiff behavior.","Add workflow regressions proving exact quoted paths reach changedPaths and reports, with deleted paths still excluded and rename destinations retained.","Run gofmt -w cmd internal, go vet ./..., and go test ./...; report any unavailable check exactly rather than recording it as passed."],"consequences":"Live candidate reports, scoped preflight inputs, and decision path records will retain Git’s exact pathname bytes even when textual diffs quote them. File counts, statuses, rename representation, deletion filtering, awareness counting, and report disclaimers keep their existing meanings. A diff/path-set disagreement becomes an explicit failure instead of silently omitting a file.","files":["internal/report/report.go","internal/report/report_test.go","internal/workflow/engine.go","internal/workflow/engine_test.go"],"mode":"modify","related_invariants":["sensei_code.report.states_what_it_does_not_establish","sensei_code.candidate.disposition_is_decided_and_evidence_outlives_removal","sensei_code.workflow.context_never_widens_worker_scope"],"plan":"Add an exact-path-aware report constructor that combines a candidate diff’s presentation metadata with gitx.Capture.Paths as the authoritative pathname set. It must preserve one FileChange per logical change, including Added, Modified, Deleted, Renamed, and OldPath; a rename consumes both exact paths but remains one Renamed FileChange. Any mismatch between the diff structure and exact path set must fail closed. Keep FromDiff available for existing parser-only consumers. In the workflow, construct one Change from the final capture and reuse it for reporting and changedPaths, with deleted files still excluded from the post-change path list. Do not alter report disclaimers, governance counts, admission semantics, or unrelated workflow behavior. The task-scoped briefing must be retried once Sensei Code creates the task session; the current exact MCP error was: tool call error: tool call failed for `sensei/task_briefing`; Caused by: Mcp error: -32000: no task session exists in this repository.","claims":[{"statement":"gitx.Capture.Paths is populated from `git diff --name-status -z` after artifact exclusions, without trimming, whitespace splitting, or rename detection.","about":"internal/gitx/capture.go","source":"repository"},{"statement":"report.FromDiff currently derives FileChange paths from textual diff headers and therefore misses or misreads Git-quoted pathnames.","about":"internal/report/report.go","source":"repository"},{"statement":"report.Change represents logical file changes with status and optional rename OldPath, and existing consumers depend on those semantics.","about":"internal/report/report.go and internal/workflow/routine.go","source":"repository"},{"statement":"emitChangeReport and changedPaths currently reparse diff text through report.FromDiff even though runCandidate already holds a gitx.Capture.","about":"internal/workflow/engine.go","source":"repository"},{"statement":"Sensei classifies the four-file scope as ARCHITECTURE_SENSITIVE with high confidence, local blast radius, and no approval gate.","about":"planned report and workflow files","source":"graph"},{"statement":"Every report must continue to end with the claims it is not entitled to make.","about":"internal/report/report.go","source":"graph"},{"statement":"The planned regression-test files already exist, so this plan creates no new surfaces.","about":"internal/report/report_test.go and internal/workflow/engine_test.go","source":"repository"}],"plan_source":"architect"}}
