{"id":"20260830T054143.269728662Z-b24c1f5e","time":"2026-08-30T05:41:43.269728662Z","session_id":"session-20260830T052251.276503861Z","task_id":"task-1788067371276752033","source":"claude","kind":"output","summary":"{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01RAyGAcGBUv7nvcDhPdjNih\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\" M internal/report/report.go\\n M internal/report/report_test.go\\n M internal/workflow/engine.go\\n?? internal/workflow/exactpaths_test.go\\n internal/report/report.go      | 284 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++---\\n internal/report/report_test.go | 221 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++\\n internal/workflow/engine.go    |  64 +++++++---\\n 3 files changed, 533 insertions(+), 36 deletions(-)\",\"is_error\":false}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"afed017a-2ac9-46ae-8762-8a00ce03dcf8\",\"uuid\":\"656b4b58-c650-4358-b406-9d2da5a0e1e9\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-30T05:41:43.268Z\",\"tool_use_result\":{\"stdout\":\" M internal/report/report.go\\n M internal/report/report_test.go\\n M internal/workflow/engine.go\\n?? internal/workflow/exactpaths_test.go\\n internal/report/report.go      | 284 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++---\\n internal/report/report_test.go | 221 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++\\n internal/workflow/engine.go    |  64 +++++++---\\n 3 files changed, 533 insertions(+), 36 deletions(-)\",\"stderr\":\"\",\"interrupted\":false,\"isImage\":false,\"noOutputExpected\":false}}","payload":{"stream":"stdout"}}
{"id":"20260830T054211.717780233Z-9407f015","time":"2026-08-30T05:42:11.717780233Z","session_id":"session-20260830T052251.276503861Z","task_id":"task-1788067371276752033","source":"claude","kind":"output","summary":"{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011CeYQ4FHmDJPMd6vFg5t44\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Implemented the bounded plan.\\n\\n**What changed**\\n\\n`internal/report/report.go`\\n- `FromDiff` and the new `FromCapture(diff string, paths []string) (Change, error)` now share one `scanDiff` pass that records what each diff entry says about itself (status, rename lines, header, added governance-entry count) without resolving pathnames. `FromDiff` resolves them the way it always did — same text, same behavior — and its doc now says it is lossy for names Git quotes.\\n- `FromCapture` takes the pathname bytes from the capture's measured set: it undoes Git's C-style quoting (`unquotePath`/`splitQuoted`, decoding to **bytes**, not through `strconv.Unquote`, which would turn a non-UTF-8 byte into U+FFFD), then requires each entry's b-side to be a path the capture measured. It fails closed both ways: a diff entry naming an unmeasured path, and a measured path no entry claims. Rename detection is on in the diff and off in the path set, so a rename stays **one** `Renamed` `FileChange` that consumes both exact paths and keeps `OldPath`. Status semantics, awareness counting, `Render`, and `NotEstablished` are untouched.\\n\\n`internal/workflow/engine.go`\\n- `changedPathsOf(report.Change)` is the list of files that exist afterwards; `changedPaths(diff)` now calls it through `FromDiff` for the parser-only callers (`ChangedPathsIn`, the inspect-mode message, the observation scan) and is documented as lossy.\\n- `e.exactChange(taskID, diff, capture.Paths)` builds the shape once from the final capture; `emitChangeReport` now receives that `Change` instead of re-parsing the diff, and `recordDecision` reuses the same one, so report and decision name the same files.\\n\\n**One judgement call I made, and its cost.** `FromCapture` fails closed, but the engine does not fail the run with it: at that point the candidate has already been reviewed and accepted, and validation re-reads the *diff* after formatters run while `capture.Paths` was measured before — so a formatter that adds or removes a file would make the two disagree. `exactChange` emits the exact error as a Status event and falls back to `FromDiff`, never substituting silently. Failing the accepted run there would have been a larger workflow behavior change than the plan authorizes; if you want it to fail instead, that's a one-line change.\\n\\n**Tests** (all new report/workflow tests pass; the workflow one is a genuine falsifier — stubbing `exactChange` back to `FromDiff` fails it with `[\\\"\\\\\\\"re\\\\\\\\tnamed.go\\\\\\\"\\\"]`, the quoted addition missing entirely)\\n- `internal/report/report_test.go`: tab, newline, quote and non-UTF-8 pathnames through `FromCapture`; a companion test pinning that `FromDiff` loses exactly those; ordinary paths, a space path, and the header nobody can split by searching (`a/b/confusing a/name.txt b/b/confusing a/name.txt`); a deletion at a quoted path; a rename consuming both exact paths; both mismatch directions; agreement with `FromDiff` on ordinary paths; governance counted under a quoted awareness path.\\n- `internal/workflow/exactpaths_test.go`: a real Git repo whose candidate adds `quo\\\"ted\\\\tpath.go`, deletes a file and renames to `re\\\\tnamed.go` — asserts the exact paths reach `changedPathsOf`, the deleted path does not, the rename keeps `Path`/`OldPath`, and that Git's own diff agrees with Git's own path set. A second test pins the wiring (the accept branch goes through `e.exactChange(… capture.Paths)`; `emitChangeReport` no longer calls `FromDiff`).\\n\\nI also stress-ran the parser against real Git output for 19 files (backslash, leading quote, trailing space, nested spacey directories, non-UTF-8, two renames — 21 measured paths) and every name came through byte-exact; that scratch test was removed.\\n\\n**Checks**\\n- `gofmt -w cmd internal` — clean.\\n- `go vet ./...` — clean.\\n- `go test ./...` — everything passes **except** `internal/publish`: `TestCommitAndPushReachARealRemote` and `TestPublicationPushesTheObjectNotTheRefThatNamedIt` fail with `sensei-code: push is refused; publication is human-owned and the push capability is not granted`. That is this worker environment's capability guard, not this change: I extracted the base commit (`git archive HEAD`) into a clean tree and both fail identically there. Those two checks **could not run here**; I am not recording them as passed.\\n\\n**Left undone deliberately.** The conversation's `sensei propose` convention would have this fixed error class recorded as a failure_mode/required_test scar, but the plan does not contain it and it writes to governance YAML — your call, not mine. `internal/workflow/prospective.go`, `testedit.go`, `routine.go` and the inspect-mode `changedPaths(diff)` message still use the parser-only route; they hold a diff and no capture, so making them exact is a different change.\\n\\nSensei: preflight over both files returns `ARCHITECTURE_SENSITIVE`, blast radius local, approval gate none; `awareness_edit_check` on `internal/report/report.go` returned 0 rules, no warnings. The task-scoped `sensei/task_briefing` retry the plan asked for still fails with the same exact error: `tool call error: tool call failed for 'sensei/task_briefing'; Caused by: Mcp error: -32000: no task session exists in this repository` — no task session exists yet.\\n\\nAWG: briefing(internal/report/report.go, internal/workflow/engine.go) | invariants: sensei_code.report.states_what_it_does_not_establish (report disclaimers untouched), sensei_code.candidate.disposition_is_decided_and_evidence_outlives_removal (no disposition path touched) | uncertainty: whether the engine should fail the accepted run on a capture/diff disagreement rather than report the fallback out loud\"}],\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":677,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":139213,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":677},\"output_tokens\":2,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"not_available\"},\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"afed017a-2ac9-46ae-8762-8a00ce03dcf8\",\"uuid\":\"824255e4-e493-4362-ac7b-886e56508bbf\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-30T05:42:11.703Z\",\"request_id\":\"req_011CeYQ4EQRz6mYWdGko6ZCH\"}","payload":{"stream":"stdout"}}
